Provenance: the part of Linux From Scratch's expect-5.45.4-gcc15-1.patch that
  Debian's patches (debian-*.patch, applied first) do not already make.
  https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/patches/lfs/development/expect-5.45.4-gcc15-1.patch
  sha256 ab5fc0af9e2e0f80d7623c1a3a3dbeb1da3d8c9134276792199df401f9eb2cec
  (Xi Ruoyao, 2025-04-21; from Fedora's covscan/c99 patches plus C23 fixes.
  It was the whole patch until the Tcl 9 port; mirrored as
  gs://minimal-staging-archives/expect-5.45.4-gcc15-1.patch.)
  Produced by applying the LFS patch on top of the Debian series and keeping
  the hunks that applied; every hunk that did not apply makes a change Debian
  already makes (prototypes, exp_deleteProc, the channel type). What is left:
  the configure C99 test programs (int main, no implicit exit), the
  exp_background_channelhandler prototype, va_end on early returns, <pty.h>.
License: these are the LFS patch's own lines, carried as before (this recipe has
  applied the whole LFS patch since its gcc 15 fix); expect itself is a NIST
  work in the public domain.
END-OF-PROVENANCE
